Compiling GNU Make inside /sources

1. Navigate to the sources directory and download GNU Make:

`cd /sources`
`curl -O https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/make/make-4.4.1.tar.gz`

2. Extract the archive and enter the build directory:

`tar -xf make-4.4.1.tar.gz`
`cd make-4.4.1`

3. Configure, compile, and install GNU Make:

`./configure --prefix=/usr --disable-nls`
`make -j$(nproc)`
`make install`

4. Clean up the build workspace:

`cd /sources`
`rm -rf make-4.4.1`
